WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:01.987
[Woman]- Filet mignon
is a really wonderful

00:00:01.987 --> 00:00:03.651
high quality piece of steak.

00:00:03.651 --> 00:00:05.257
It's a bit pricier than other cuts,

00:00:05.257 --> 00:00:07.098
so it can be a little intimidating.

00:00:07.098 --> 00:00:09.175
But whether you're splurging
for a special occasion

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:10.982
or just honing in on your skills,

00:00:10.982 --> 00:00:12.873
here's a few foolproof ways to make sure

00:00:12.873 --> 00:00:15.142
you get it right and
get the most out of it.

00:00:15.142 --> 00:00:19.296
(slow jazz electric guitar)

00:00:19.296 --> 00:00:20.815
30 minutes before you start cooking

00:00:20.815 --> 00:00:22.333
you want to take your
steak out of the fridge

00:00:22.333 --> 00:00:24.209
and let it rest at room temperature.

00:00:24.209 --> 00:00:25.644
If you grab it straight from the fridge

00:00:25.644 --> 00:00:27.178
and throw a cold steak in a hot pan,

00:00:27.178 --> 00:00:29.028
it'll bring down the pan's temperature

00:00:29.028 --> 00:00:31.048
and you won't get that great crust.

00:00:31.048 --> 00:00:33.511
Next you want to pat your
steak dry with paper towel.

00:00:33.511 --> 00:00:35.317
This will absorb any excess moisture

00:00:35.317 --> 00:00:38.049
that could keep the steak
from getting an even crust.

00:00:38.049 --> 00:00:40.724
So, then you want to really
generously season the steak

00:00:40.724 --> 00:00:42.763
with coarse salt and pepper.

00:00:42.763 --> 00:00:45.131
This might seem like an
aggressive amount of seasoning

00:00:45.131 --> 00:00:46.514
but you really need that much

00:00:46.514 --> 00:00:48.463
to get the flavor throughout the steak.

00:00:48.463 --> 00:00:51.141
And don't forget to cover every side.

00:00:51.141 --> 00:00:52.376
Next, we're going to sear the steak.

00:00:52.376 --> 00:00:54.893
For searing, you should
use a stainless steel

00:00:54.893 --> 00:00:56.948
or cast iron pan,
because they're oven safe

00:00:56.948 --> 00:00:59.352
and can maintain a high, steady heat

00:00:59.352 --> 00:01:02.012
which you need to get
a really great crust.

00:01:02.012 --> 00:01:04.863
Heat the pan over high heat
for about five minutes.

00:01:04.863 --> 00:01:06.385
You can actually feel the heat

00:01:06.385 --> 00:01:07.949
coming off the pan when it's ready.

00:01:07.949 --> 00:01:09.446
Then we're going to add

00:01:09.446 --> 00:01:10.903
a neutral oil with a high smoke point.

00:01:10.903 --> 00:01:12.388
We use grapeseed oil,
but you could also use

00:01:12.388 --> 00:01:15.311
canola, vegetable or even sunflower oil.

00:01:15.311 --> 00:01:17.837
Once you see the oil start
to shimmer like this,

00:01:17.837 --> 00:01:19.108
and it's starting to smoke,

00:01:19.108 --> 00:01:21.692
that's when you know you're
ready to start searing.

00:01:21.692 --> 00:01:22.857
Place the filet in the pan and let it sit

00:01:22.857 --> 00:01:25.212
for two to three minutes
without moving it.

00:01:25.212 --> 00:01:27.143
Seriously don't move it.

00:01:27.143 --> 00:01:28.411
That's going to allow it to form

00:01:28.411 --> 00:01:29.936
this really great crust,

00:01:29.936 --> 00:01:32.245
also known as that maillard reaction.

00:01:32.245 --> 00:01:34.581
After that crust is
formed, flip your steak.

00:01:34.581 --> 00:01:35.810
If it's sticking to the pan,

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:37.592
that just means it's not ready yet,

00:01:37.592 --> 00:01:40.616
and you should let it keep
searing until it self-releases.

00:01:40.616 --> 00:01:43.002
If you really want to enhance
the flavor of your steak,

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:44.228
you can baste it.

00:01:44.228 --> 00:01:45.877
To baste, you want to
add a couple tablespoons

00:01:45.877 --> 00:01:48.725
of butter along with some
herbs and garlic to the pan.

00:01:48.725 --> 00:01:51.143
Then you tilt the pan so the
butter pools on one side,

00:01:51.143 --> 00:01:53.428
and continuously spoon that herby butter

00:01:53.428 --> 00:01:55.878
over the steak for one to two minutes.

00:01:55.878 --> 00:01:57.899
This process is a really quick step

00:01:57.899 --> 00:02:00.324
to infuse your steak
with even more flavor.

00:02:00.324 --> 00:02:02.606
Trust us, you should try it.

00:02:02.606 --> 00:02:04.517
So, we're going to finish
our steak off in the oven

00:02:04.517 --> 00:02:07.201
because it's the easiest way
to guarantee an even cook.

00:02:07.201 --> 00:02:10.031
Place the pan in a pre-heated
oven of 450 degrees.

00:02:10.031 --> 00:02:12.767
Seven minutes will get
you a perfectly done

00:02:12.767 --> 00:02:15.050
medium rare filet, which
is what we'd recommend.

00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:17.712
It should be 130 degrees when
you take it out of the oven.

00:02:17.712 --> 00:02:20.748
After letting it rest, the
temperature will go up to 135.

00:02:20.748 --> 00:02:22.279
If you prefer a different cook,

00:02:22.279 --> 00:02:24.435
you can adjust the amount
of time in the oven.

00:02:24.435 --> 00:02:26.092
We prefer medium rare because

00:02:26.092 --> 00:02:27.730
well, your steak is going to stay

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:29.396
really tender and flavorful.

00:02:29.396 --> 00:02:30.697
Then you want to let it rest

00:02:30.697 --> 00:02:32.429
at room temperature for about ten minutes

00:02:32.429 --> 00:02:34.661
to make sure it stays tender and juicy.

00:02:34.661 --> 00:02:35.852
If you slice it right away,

00:02:35.852 --> 00:02:37.035
the juices will run out,

00:02:37.035 --> 00:02:38.791
which can dry out your steak.

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:40.274
When you let it rest the juices

00:02:40.274 --> 00:02:41.946
will absorb evenly throughout the steak,

00:02:41.946 --> 00:02:42.958
keeping it tender.

00:02:42.958 --> 00:02:44.605
The temperature will continue to rise

00:02:44.605 --> 00:02:47.612
by about five degrees while it's resting.

00:02:47.612 --> 00:02:50.427
With any steak, you want to
slice it against the grain.

00:02:50.427 --> 00:02:53.001
Filet Mignon is already a
really tender cut of steak,

00:02:53.001 --> 00:02:54.946
but this is just an extra tip to make sure

00:02:54.946 --> 00:02:57.480
it's the best it can be.

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:58.945
And that's all it takes!

00:02:58.945 --> 00:03:01.267
Filet mignon is a really
wonderful cut of meat,

00:03:01.267 --> 00:03:02.677
but it can be pretty intimidating

00:03:02.677 --> 00:03:04.099
because of it's price point.

00:03:04.099 --> 00:03:06.582
But when you want a
splurge, give it a try!

00:03:06.582 --> 00:03:08.344
It's not fundamentally harder to cook

00:03:08.344 --> 00:03:09.828
than any other cuts of steak,

00:03:09.828 --> 00:03:11.294
the same principals apply.

00:03:11.294 --> 00:03:13.030
And with these few tips in mind,

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:16.472
you're guaranteed to get a
restaurant-quality steak at home.

00:03:16.472 --> 00:03:18.445
(slow jazz piano)

00:03:18.445 --> 00:03:20.578
I mean you can make it for your spouse...

00:03:20.578 --> 00:03:23.894
For yourself... I've made
it for myself many times.

00:03:23.894 --> 00:03:25.389
If you're trying to woo someone.

00:03:25.389 --> 00:03:26.944
[Other Woman]- It's a good woo

00:03:26.944 --> 00:03:28.750
[Woman]- It's a good woo technique!

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:29.841
(laughs)

00:03:29.841 --> 00:03:31.563
It's a good woo steak!

00:03:31.563 --> 00:03:34.313
(camera shutter)

